# Static assets are meant to be publicly served (CSS/JS/images), so access is allowed here —
# but harden the directory: no directory listing and never execute server-side code out of it
# (defence-in-depth against an uploaded/planted script ever landing under assets/).
Options -Indexes

<FilesMatch "\.(php|phtml|php[0-9]|phar|pht|cgi|pl|py|sh)$">
    <IfModule mod_authz_core.c>
        Require all denied
    </IfModule>
    <IfModule !mod_authz_core.c>
        Order deny,allow
        Deny from all
    </IfModule>
</FilesMatch>

# Caching (1.74.0, PERF-7). Measured on production before this: no Cache-Control at all on assets/, so a
# browser revalidated on a guess (a tenth of the file's age), and the revalidation then FAILED — 20 of 22
# files came back 200 with the whole body (~410 KB gzip) instead of 304.
#
# 1. An address with a version (`?v=<mtime>`, assetVer() in includes/functions.php — every stylesheet and
#    script a page links) never changes what it answers: a changed file is a changed address. A year,
#    immutable — not even revalidated. ONLY those: the favicon and what scripts fetch by a bare path
#    (assets/img/favicon.svg, assets/emoji/…) carry no version, and a year of immutable would freeze them.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
    <If "%{QUERY_STRING} =~ /(^|&)v=/">
        Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
    </If>
</IfModule>
# 2. Why the revalidation failed: mod_deflate appends `-gzip` to the ETag of a compressed answer, the
#    browser sends that tag back in If-None-Match, and Apache does not recognise its own tag with the
#    suffix — so it answers 200 with everything. Without an ETag the browser revalidates by
#    Last-Modified, which compression does not touch: 304. (iconpack.php, which sends its own ETag, takes
#    the suffix off before comparing — includes/iconpack.php, iconpackRequestEtags().)
FileETag None
